             headline='Undeclared gathering at Place de la République on Sunday afternoon: police used tear gas at about 15:34, and the prefecture calls the gathering undeclared. Crowd estimates range from dozens to about 1,000 (a police source to CNews), I found no arrest count, and nothing after 15:39, so expect police around République and the Élysée. President Macron holds a crisis meeting at 17:30 and addresses the French on TF1 and LCI at 20:00. Other disruption today is transport and roads: métro line 6 is closed all day, the Vincennes half marathon closed forest roads from 08:30 to noon, and the République stop of line 8 and the Saint-Michel stop of line 4 are not served because of long works. I found no new gathering ban or station closure for Sunday.',
